   417	## 6. Human-parameter injection: unresolved means no default
   418	
   419	### 6.1 Required representation
   420	
   421	```ts
   422	type Unresolved = {
   423	  status: "UNRESOLVED";
   424	  owner: "V";
   425	  value?: never;       // absence is deliberate; null/0/false are not substitutes
   426	  expectedType: string; // descriptive schema reference, never a selected choice
   427	};
   428	
   429	type Resolved<T> = {
   430	  status: "RESOLVED";
   431	  owner: "V";
   432	  value: T;
   433	  decidedAt: ISODateTime;
   434	  decisionArtifact: ArtifactRef;
   435	};
   436	
   437	type HumanValue<T> = Unresolved | Resolved<T>;
   438	
   439	interface HumanPolicyState {
   440	  engineRelationship: HumanValue<"REPLACE" | "WRAP" | "SUPERSEDE_OLD_CHECKLIST_ONLY">;
   441	  queryAmendment: HumanValue<{
   442	    mode: "ABSOLUTE" | "VERSIONED_EXPLORATORY" | "OFF_SET_INADMISSIBLE";
   443	    amendmentMaySupportConfirmatoryClaim: boolean;
   444	  }>;
   445	  subjectRelevance: HumanValue<"BINARY" | "WHOLE_BINARY_PARTIAL_GRADED" | "GRADED">;
   446	  abstention: HumanValue<{
   447	    lowEndpointMeaning: string; highEndpointMeaning: string;
   448	    price: number; scope: "GLOBAL" | "BY_QUESTION_CLASS";
   449	  }>;
   450	  lineageEquivalence: HumanValue<{
   451	    sameMakerGenerations: "SAME" | "DISTINCT" | "RELATION_MATRIX";
   452	    sharedBaseModelRule: string; providerRule: string;
   453	  }>;
   454	  criticUnavailable: HumanValue<"LABEL_AND_PROCEED" | "HOLD_PROVISIONAL" | "BLOCK_CONFIDENT_BAND">;
   455	  newHumanRules: HumanValue<Record<"R6" | "R7" | "R8" | "R9", {
   456	    disposition: "ACCEPT" | "AMEND" | "REJECT"; enforcementText?: string;
   457	  }>>;
   458	  comparisonValueOwnership: HumanValue<{
   459	    ownerRole: string; weightSource: string; acceptedOutput: "PARETO" | "CONDITIONAL" | "OWNER_WEIGHTS";
   460	  }>;
   461	  splitIterationLimit: HumanValue<{ regenerationRounds: number; critiqueRounds: number }>;
   462	  orderingPolicy: HumanValue<"RETRIEVE_MEASURE_THEN_SPLIT" | "SPLIT_THEN_RETRIEVE" | "EXPERIMENTAL_RANDOMIZED">;
   463	  livenessThreshold: HumanValue<{
   464	    minimumRuns: number; requiredQuestionClasses: string[];
   465	    demoteCriterion: string; removeCriterion: string;
   466	  }>;
   467	  expiryPolicy: HumanValue<
   468	    | { mode: "NO_AUTOMATIC_EXPIRY" }
   469	    | { mode: "RISK_VOLATILITY"; ruleArtifact: ArtifactRef }
   470	  >;
   471	  citationEnforcement: HumanValue<{
   472	    checkerRequirement: string; hardKillConditions: string[];
   473	    automationRequiredBeforeHardKill: boolean;
   474	  }>;
   475	  coverageUpgrade: HumanValue<
   476	    | { mode: "DIAGNOSTIC_ONLY" }
   477	    | { mode: "VALIDATED_GATE"; mechanismArtifact: ArtifactRef; validationArtifact: ArtifactRef }
   478	  >;
   479	  graphMeasurementQuota: HumanValue<"AUTHORIZE" | "DO_NOT_AUTHORIZE">;
   480	  stage11Rollout: HumanValue<"DAY_ONE" | "PHASED" | "DEFER_FULL_SETTLE">;
   481	  adoptionBar: HumanValue<{
   482	    baseline: string; questionSet: ArtifactRef; matchedCostRule: string;
   483	    outcomeMetrics: string[]; minimumThresholds: Record<string, number>;
   484	  }>;
   485	}
   486	```
   487	
   488	Validation constraints: `0 < abstention.price < 1`; iteration limits are non-negative integers and at least one stopping alternative must exist; no `VALIDATED_GATE` mode is legal without both referenced artifacts; no policy may be inferred from an omitted field. The two concrete split-loop counts mentioned in the plan are unverified proposals, not defaults.
   489	
   490	### 6.2 Open decisions and their injection points
   491	
   492	| Parameter | Why V owns it | First consumer | Behavior while unresolved |
   493	|---|---|---|---|
   494	| `engineRelationship` | Opening plan explicitly reserves replace/wrap/checklist-only relationship. | Product architecture, outside a battery run. | No migration/integration inference. |
   495	| `queryAmendment` | Human Rule 1 may only be loosened by its owner. | R1/Q11/Q15. | Off-plan retrieval cannot silently support a claim; implementation remains policy-blocked at amendment. |
   496	| `subjectRelevance` | Binary versus graded enforcement is a Part 6 human decision. | R2/Q32. | Clear whole mismatch is rejected; partial evidence remains unresolved and cannot silently receive weight. |
   497	| `abstention` | Scale meanings and price are value/product choices with no empirical default. | Q6/Q56. | Mark `UNPRICED`; Q56 cannot run. |
   498	| `lineageEquivalence` | Glossary leaves same-maker generations/shared bases unresolved. | Q14/Q31/Q39/R5/R6. | Do not certify independence. |
   499	| `criticUnavailable` | Plan records three live enforcement positions. | Q14/Q39/R5. | Always label missing critic; no implicit confident-band policy. |
   500	| `newHumanRules` | R6–R9 are owner-added and unreviewed. | R6 at intake through R9 at serve. | Preserve as proposed requirements, not approved production law. |
   501	| `comparisonValueOwnership` | An LLM cannot manufacture criterion weights or normative winner. | Q50/Q57. | Serve vector/Pareto/conditional only; route owner-dependent choice. |
   502	| `splitIterationLimit` | Cap is mandatory, but proposed numeric counts were unverified reasoning. | Q6/Q26/Q29/Q31. | Stage 6 cannot enter a regenerative loop. |
   503	| `orderingPolicy` | Retrieve-first versus split-first is genuinely contested upstream. | T4–T6 scheduler. | Architecture records proposed order but cannot call it settled law. |
   504	| `livenessThreshold` | Q62 supplies law, not sample size/class coverage. | Q62. | Count liveness; do not demote/remove. |
   505	| `expiryPolicy` | No designer supplied a working decay mechanism. | Q18/Q58/Q59 and monitoring. | Freshness checked at run; revision trigger shown; no automatic expiry claim. |
   506	| `citationEnforcement` | Hard-kill positions differ and universal automation is absent. | Q16/Q40/Q51. | Enforce known exact/preview/locator rules and named checking; do not claim universal gate. |
   507	| `coverageUpgrade` | Coverage is mandatory in intent but no working gate exists. | Q27 and any future coverage gate. | Diagnostic residual only; never certify completeness. |
   508	| `graphMeasurementQuota` | One standing authorization is needed for graph-level evidence. | Validation and engine experiments. | Record quota blocker; no fabricated result. |
   509	| `stage11Rollout` | Full SETTLE is weakest-attested and day-one scope is undecided. | T11 deployment. | Keep contracts and persistence design; do not claim operational calibration. |
   510	| `adoptionBar` | No battery has been compared against a baseline; superiority threshold is a product decision. | Validation gate. | No production/adoption/superiority claim. |
   511	
   512	Per-run human inputs are separate from V's global policy: decision/action owner for Q1, normative owner for Q7/Q50/Q57, owner-supplied comparison weights, caller scope/as-of date, and external resolver for Q59. A model may format these values; it may not create them.
