+REVIEW LENS HANDOFF COMPLETE
+Lens: machine-executability/spec-precision (Codex)
+Verdict: LENS CHANGES REQUESTED
+
+Findings:
+
+1. **blocker — The map does not assign production of all four destination artifacts.**
+   - **Exact file + section:** `wayfinder/map.md`, `Destination` and `Notes` / `Execution override` (lines 7–14, 41–43); `wayfinder/issues/02-scoring-behavior-extraction.md`, `Deliverable`; `wayfinder/issues/04-node-graph-data-model.md`, `Deliverable`; `wayfinder/issues/15-race-victory-criteria.md`, `Settles`; `wayfinder/issues/16-ui-flex-negotiation.md`, `Question`.
+   - **Evidence:** The destination promises (1) a requirements spec, (2) a clean-room carryover manifest, (3) a V2-UI boundary contract, and (4) race/victory criteria. No ticket produces artifacts 1 or 2: tickets 02 and 04 produce research inputs under `research/`, not either destination document. Tickets 16 and 15 say their answers *are* or *settle* artifacts 3 and 4, but name no output path, required document shape, completion test, or review/assembly handoff. There is also no spec-pack assembly ticket. An ARCHITECTURE author must therefore invent authorship, paths, merge order, and what “complete” means.
+   - **Concrete change:** Add an explicit producing ticket for each destination artifact (or an explicitly bounded combined authoring ticket). Each producer must name the exact artifact path, prerequisite tickets, inputs, required sections and traceability, Definition of Done, and review gate. Make the final spec-pack gate depend on all four producer tickets and their lens reviews.
+
+2. **blocker — The 05 → 07/08 coverage law has a broken edge and no row-level closure gate.**
+   - **Exact file + section:** `wayfinder/issues/05-battery-coverage-matrix.md`, `Why`, `Scope`, and `Deliverable` (lines 13–38); `wayfinder/issues/07-ratify-unanimous-batch.md`, `Blocked by`, `Method`, and `Settles`; `wayfinder/issues/08-contested-cluster-rulings.md`, `Blocked by`, `Method`, and `Settles`.
+   - **Evidence:** Ticket 05 explicitly says tickets 07 **and 08** consume its matrix, but ticket 08 is blocked only by 06. It can therefore be worked without the authoritative 71-row roster or the matrix's spec-section mapping. Tickets 07 and 08 have no deliverable and no obligation to write their V rulings back to a canonical ledger. The arithmetic is consistent at headline level (07 claims 38 Q + 5 R; 08 claims 24 Q + 4 R), but a row may still be omitted, duplicated, left conditional without an owner, or merely assigned a section name while that section contains no normative requirement. Both tickets can close with decisions existing only in comments, so “all 62+9 covered” is not machine-checkable.
+   - **Concrete change:** Make 08 `Blocked by: 05, 06`. Define one canonical coverage ledger with, at minimum, `row_id`, upstream row-contract reference, final V disposition, conditions, decision-record ID, destination artifact/requirement ID, and closure state. Require 07 and the per-theme successors of 08 to update that ledger. Add a gate that fails unless Q1–Q62 and R1–R9 each appear exactly once, have final V authority or an explicit accepted deferral, and point to substantive requirement text in the produced spec.
+
+3. **major — Several upstream human-owned parameters have no decision ticket or explicit accepted deferral.**
+   - **Exact file + section:** upstream `reports/report-for-llm-agents.md`, `6.1 Required representation` and `6.2 Open decisions and their injection points` (especially lines 461–480 and 502–510); `wayfinder/issues/05-battery-coverage-matrix.md`, `Scope` (lines 21–28); `wayfinder/issues/12-human-rules-and-knobs.md`, `Question`.
+   - **Evidence:** The upstream executable contract declares `splitIterationLimit`, `citationEnforcement`, `coverageUpgrade`, and `graphMeasurementQuota` as unresolved V-owned parameters with distinct consumers and unresolved behavior. No charted ticket names the first three. Ticket 12's phrase “per-question quota” does not identify `graphMeasurementQuota`, its units, or its authorization semantics. Ticket 05 says it will list every unresolved parameter “with its owning ticket,” but supplies no route or failure rule when no owner exists. A matrix can expose these orphans but cannot settle them, leaving ARCHITECTURE to default or defer them by guess.
+   - **Concrete change:** Give every upstream human parameter exactly one decision owner, or record an explicit V-approved deferral with the precise behavior while unresolved. Add to ticket 05: an ownerless parameter is a blocking result that causes creation of a named grilling ticket before coverage closure. Use the upstream parameter names and first-consumer semantics verbatim or provide an explicit old→new mapping.
+
+4. **major — The grilling topology is not single-decision and has no deterministic split protocol.**
+   - **Exact file + section:** `wayfinder/map.md`, `Notes` / method and pace (lines 18–23); `wayfinder/issues/07-ratify-unanimous-batch.md`, `Question` and `Method`; `wayfinder/issues/08-contested-cluster-rulings.md`, `Question` and `Method`; `wayfinder/issues/09-evidence-policy.md`, `Question`; `wayfinder/issues/10-abstention-semantics.md`, `Question`; `wayfinder/issues/12-human-rules-and-knobs.md`, `Question`; `wayfinder/issues/14-staleness-expiry-policy.md`, `Question`; `wayfinder/issues/15-race-victory-criteria.md`, `Question` and `Inputs`.
+   - **Evidence:** The map says one question at a time, but 08 contains an unknown number of themed and row rulings and only *may* split, without a split criterion or ticket-creation owner. Ticket 07 can create arbitrary “on the spot” exceptions without stable IDs. Tickets 09, 10, 12, 14, and 15 each bundle independently answerable policies; ticket 12 alone combines four rule dispositions with at least five unrelated knobs, while 15 combines metric selection, workload mix, matched-cost law, thresholds, promotion mode, production-validation bar, and Stage-11 rollout. Different sittings can partially close or contradict one another, and status cannot state which subdecision remains open.
+   - **Concrete change:** Split these into one-decision tickets with stable IDs and explicit dependencies. Make 08's per-theme fanout mandatory after 06, with each successor listing the exact Q/R rows it owns. Allow 07 to remain a batch only for one atomic “adopt all listed rows unchanged” ruling; every exception must become a separately tracked decision before 07 closes. Give each decision an explicit option schema, output record, and closure condition.
+
+5. **major — R6–R9 can receive conflicting normative and implementation rulings.**
+   - **Exact file + section:** `wayfinder/issues/07-ratify-unanimous-batch.md`, `Question` and `Settles`; `wayfinder/issues/08-contested-cluster-rulings.md`, `Question` and `Settles`; `wayfinder/issues/12-human-rules-and-knobs.md`, `Question`; upstream `reports/report-for-llm-agents.md`, `HumanPolicyState.newHumanRules` (lines 455–457) and `Human-rule merged contracts` (lines 355–369).
+   - **Evidence:** Ticket 07 may adopt R7 and R9 “as spec law,” and ticket 08 may classify R6 and R8, while ticket 12 independently asks whether the same four new rules are accepted. None blocks on another. Upstream requires an `ACCEPT | AMEND | REJECT` disposition per rule, but ticket 12 offers “accepted unchanged, or reviewed first”; “reviewed first” is a process step, not a terminal disposition. A rule can thus be counted as coverage-complete and implementation-classified, then amended or rejected elsewhere.
+   - **Concrete change:** Split R6–R9 normative ratification into four terminal decision tickets with `ACCEPT`, `AMEND` (including final text), and `REJECT`. Make their implementation-classification/coverage rows depend on those outcomes, or state formally that 07/08 decisions are conditional and cannot close the rule rows until ratification is final.
+
+6. **major — The UI-boundary path has a missing dependency, contradictory option set, and no exhaustive output inventory.**
+   - **Exact file + section:** `wayfinder/map.md`, `Not yet specified` (lines 74–76 and 86–88); `wayfinder/issues/01-ui-boundary-contract-map.md`, `Why`; `wayfinder/issues/16-ui-flex-negotiation.md`, `Blocked by`, `Question`, `Inputs`, and `Guard`.
+   - **Evidence:** The map says mapping the five abstentions to UI affordances depends on 01 **and 10**, but ticket 16 is blocked only by 01. Ticket 16 also decides value-weight markers without depending on ticket 13, which defines their ownership and meaning. The map's options include “flex vs adapt vs drop,” while ticket 16 permits only fit/adapt/small UI change, so a genuine `drop` ruling has no representable outcome. Its parenthetical battery-output list is not declared exhaustive or derived from Q1–Q62/R1–R9, and “genuinely can't express” and “small UI change” have no decision test. The resulting contract can silently omit an output or classify the same change differently in different sittings.
+   - **Concrete change:** At minimum, make 16 depend on 01, 10, and 13 (and on any rule/coverage decision that changes an exposed output). Generate an exhaustive output ledger from the 71-row spec, including non-UI outputs explicitly marked `NOT_UI_EXPOSED`. Define mutually exclusive `AS_IS | ADAPT | FLEX | DROP` outcomes, require V authority for `DROP`, and define testable criteria for information preservation and the allowed flex boundary.
+
+7. **major — Grilling decisions have no durable, machine-consumable result contract.**
+   - **Exact file + section:** `00-intake-H0.md`, `Wayfinder integration` (lines 93–102); `wayfinder/map.md`, `Decisions so far` and closed-ticket placeholder (lines 49–68); all grilling tickets 07–16, which end at `Comments` and contain no `Deliverable` section.
+   - **Evidence:** Research tickets specify exact artifact paths and handoff markers; grilling tickets do not specify whether authority lives in comments, ticket-body edits, map summaries, or future destination prose. The map's closed-ticket placeholder preserves only a “one-line gist,” which cannot encode option, conditions, affected rows, supersession, or V authority. A spec author cannot deterministically distinguish a final ruling from discussion or reconstruct which ruling supplied a requirement.
+   - **Concrete change:** Define one mandatory decision-record schema and location for every grilling ticket: decision ID, ticket ID, V-authored/confirmed option, exact normative text, conditions, affected Q/R/policy IDs, supersedes links, timestamp/authority epoch, and unresolved follow-ups. Require the map gist to link that record, and require destination requirements to cite decision IDs.
+
+8. **minor — Two conditional transitions are scheduling prose rather than executable edges.**
+   - **Exact file + section:** `wayfinder/map.md`, `Not yet specified` (lines 77–82); `wayfinder/issues/03-golden-vector-plan.md`, `Scope` and `Deliverable`; `wayfinder/issues/17-v3-repo-bootstrap.md`, `Blocked by` and `Notes`.
+   - **Evidence:** If 03 finds that a V2 harness is needed, it “graduates into a task ticket,” but no actor, trigger, required fields, or downstream blocker is named; if existing fixtures suffice, no ticket is assigned to freeze the actual `MUST-MATCH`/`MUST-DIFFER` corpus. Ticket 17 is `Blocked by: none` while instructing the runner to work it “LATE” when the pack is “nearly assembled.” A scheduler cannot evaluate either phrase, so it may run 17 immediately or proceed without the vector prerequisite implied by the clean-room promise.
+   - **Concrete change:** Give 03 a deterministic branch: either create a named harness task or a named fixture-freeze task, with both branches converging on an immutable vector-manifest deliverable consumed by the carryover artifact. Replace “LATE/nearly assembled” with explicit blockers on the relevant spec-pack producer/review tickets, or remove 17 from executable routing until those tickets exist.
+
+Refutations attempted:
+
+- I enumerated the headline coverage partition and could not break its arithmetic: 38 unanimous questions + 24 contested questions = 62, and 5 unanimous rules + 4 contested rules = 9. Ticket 06 also explicitly requires its theme union to equal the contested set.
+- I traced the nine decisions in upstream `report-for-humans.md`, `Decisions only V can make`. Intake closes #4 with `D-GREENFIELD`; tickets 09–14 visibly cover #1–#3 and #5–#9. The failure above concerns additional executable parameters declared by the companion LLM report, not those nine headline decisions.
+- I tried to orphan the two destination artifacts that do have a conceptual decision path and could not: 01→16 conceptually reaches the UI contract, and 05→15 conceptually reaches race criteria. Their missing deliverable contracts remain finding 1.
+- I checked whether the four indicted V2 semantics could be accidentally treated as carryover. The map and ticket 02 name all four consistently and mark them excluded, so that exclusion boundary survived review.
+- I checked research-ticket handoffs for path ambiguity. Tickets 01–06 each name a single research artifact and the `RESEARCH HANDOFF COMPLETE` marker; those handoffs are precise.
+
+If CHANGES REQUESTED: what proof would flip your verdict
+
+A revised map/ticket set would flip this lens only if it provides: (1) explicit producers, paths, prerequisites, and completion gates for all four destination artifacts; (2) a wired 05→07/08 canonical 71-row ledger and exactly-once closure check; (3) exactly one owner or explicit V-approved deferral for every upstream human parameter; (4) single-decision grilling tickets or deterministic fanout with durable decision records; (5) ordered, non-conflicting R6–R9 ratification/classification; (6) an exhaustive, dependency-correct UI-output disposition ledger; and (7) explicit rather than prose-only branch/scheduling edges for vector capture and repo bootstrap. A machine-generated trace showing every Q1–Q62, R1–R9, and unresolved policy mapped to one final V decision record and one substantive destination requirement would be sufficient proof of the central coverage repair.

